  "display_title": "Lapirosa at the Museum",
  "description": "Curator Jeong Hyeon-Tae tours the closed museum. While managing the museum, he receives repeated complaints that a certain statue's position keeps changing. Late one night, while closely examining the statue, he discovers it transforming into a human. Startled, he stumbles backward and accidentally shatters the world's only gem, ‘Lapirosa’. The statue, now human, makes an absurd claim: restoring Lapirosa requires gathering ‘Vitality’—an energy generated through sexual intercourse with artworks...?!\n\n(Source: Lezhin, translated)",
